[debug] Processing with CmsHarness.Web.HooksController.handle/2
  Parameters: %{"cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "PreToolUse", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "22082e4a-e3e2-45c9-812d-d39cd80412db", "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "tool_input" => %{"command" => "git add lib/code_my_spec/migration.ex lib/mix/tasks/cms.harness.onboard.ex && elixir -S mix format lib/code_my_spec/migration.ex lib/mix/tasks/cms.harness.onboard.ex 2>&1 | tail -1; git add -u && git commit -q -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nCarry each story's component across a migration\n\nexport_story never carried component_id, so every migrated story arrived\nunlinked. Requirements are computed per story and component, which means a\nfreshly migrated project reports 0/0 satisfied for everything — it reads\nas \"nothing is done\" rather than \"nothing is linked\", and there is no\namount of waiting that fixes it because the harness recomputes files and\nproblems but cannot invent the link.\n\nBy module name rather than id. Components are projections of files: each\ndeployment derives its own from the same source, so the ids differ while\nthe module name is exactly what both sides agree on — the natural key\ncomponents_module_name_project_id_index already enforces. A component\nthis deployment does not have is left unlinked rather than invented,\nsince a component conjured from a name is a fiction the requirement graph\nwould then compute against.\n\nput_rules and put_criteria are flattened on the way past; they were three\ndeep and blocking the file's credo check.\n\nAlso fixes the boundary on cms.harness.onboard, which was classified to\nCodeMySpec while using CmsHarness modules — the dependency only runs the\nother way. Worth more than tidiness: the analyzer treats any compiler\nproblem as grounds to skip exunit, credo and spex entirely, so one\nmisclassified line suppressed every other check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JPoSfcCJqSqG8iGY9nfyfL\nEOF\n)\" && git log --oneline -1", "description" => "Commit the migration and boundary fixes"}, "tool_name" => "Bash", "tool_use_id" => "toolu_01VKvnQNhBD9Y5MvRKnP41mb", "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
